Z||000000||overlord||03-22-2000||09:57 PM||||what is porting?<P>i bought 2 subwoofers and in the manual it shows all the box specs and stuff....there is only one thingg i dont get...a port.<BR>does porting affect the bass at all or what??<P>please help me..i wanna have these puppies pumpin out he toons by next week...-)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||03-22-2000||10:07 PM||||A port is like a big dock that the ships stop at.||||reg||1
Z||000002||phillip||03-23-2000||01:33 AM||||have you ever looked at a sub box with an extra hole and maybe a tube stuck in it? thats the port. usually a ported box is louder and more efficent than a sealed(no extra hole ) box, but it usually needs to be bigger. your specs will let you know. i'd make the box sealed if i could, it's simpler,but you may need more power.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||03-23-2000||09:22 AM||||Porting for subs is using the back side of the speaker to attain a lower frequency out of a specifically tuned port. This is dependent on the size of the woofer, size of port, and how you like your bass. A tight solid bass is for classical, Jazz, and hard rock generally and uses a sealed box. If your into dance/club/rap type of music then a ported box is better. With a ported box the bass has more of a "boom" and rattles everything in the car. You can also use a smaller woofer or a smaller box if box size is a concern. You will feel the vibration everywhere. Power requirements are lower for the ported box. With a sealed box the bass is sharper when the bass drum hits it'll feel like someone is hitting you in the chest. The reason you need more power with a sealed box is because it is sealed and the woofer needs to compress the air in the box. Sealed boxes tend not to distort the sound as easy as a ported box. What size woofer and what brand do you have? How much power do you plan to use? Finally what is recommended by the maker of the woofer? Some woofers are designed for a specific  application. As an example Kicker Solobarics are designed to be used in a smaller sealed box then normal for a particular size woofer.  <P>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 03-23-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 03-23-2000).]||||reg||1
