Z||000007||dogtired||03-23-2000||11:55 AM||||Must have parked my ship in the wrong place  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Did I miss something????<BR>Both Stock sub woofers I have, have the tube comming out the back top side (PORTED) ???<BR>Is there a stock sub without this (PORT)?<BR>Maybe we are talking about after-market or home made subs??      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>But this is Normal for me!   LOST   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000008||Raydar||03-23-2000||01:02 PM||||Dogtired, You're exactly right. The stock Fiero sub is ported. The long tube attached to the housing is the tuned port.  <P>Overlord, I'll see if I can find the specs on your subs, and plug them in to the program. If you have the specs, you could maybe send them to me? There are about four or five different parameters. FS, VAS, etc.<BR>Actually, your local stereo shop should be able to tell you how big the boxes need to be and how the port should be configured. Whether they WILL or not is another question.<BR>(They would probably prefer that you let THEM build the boxes.) <BR>Earlier in the thread, someone mentioned Kicker Solo-barics. Might be the better idea. They seem to require a much smaller box. As little space as we have to fool with, that may be worth investigating. Check out Crutchfield's catalog. Go to <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.crutchfield.com</A>  . Ask them for a catalog and compare the specs. The last time I checked the website, there was not a lot of info on the site. The catalog is much more useful.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||03-23-2000||01:56 PM||||A bandpass box is where the front and back of the speaker and each or one side is ported. Think of it as a subwoofer box with the speaker in the middle and just a ported hole at each or one end. You can get some nice sound but the box size is bigger because you are enclosing the front and back. The port consists of a hole with a specific tube. As an example a Pyle Drive 10" woofer in a ported box requires the port tube to be 4" long and 2" in diameter. The port size is based upon the speaker and the resonate frequency of the speaker and enclosure.<BR>For a detailed book on building sub/speaker boxes, Radio Shack sells a speaker design book for $14. It explains everything and gives you formulas to calculate an enclosure for any speaker.||||reg||1
